<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fors de Bigorre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1097</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fors de Bigorre is a charter of customary law granted around 1097 by the count of Bigorre, in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, setting out the rights of the inhabitants and limits on the count's power. Among the oldest written customs of the Pyrenees, it regulated justice, military service and relations between the count, the nobles and the free men of the valleys.</p></div>
